        "original_id": "cb1e9a68-9f41-5d75-921c-223d440337bb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: FC Dynamo Kyiv, UEFA\n- Places: Kiev, Ukraine, Olimpiyskiy National Sports Complex, Cherepanov Hill, Pechersk Raion\n- Events: UEFA Euro 2012 Final\n- Topics: Italy–Spain football rivalry\n\nFacts:\n- FC Dynamo Kyiv is a Ukrainian professional football club based in Kiev.\n- FC Dynamo Kyiv plays its home matches at the 70,050-capacity Olimpiyskiy National Sports Complex in Kiev.\n- The Olimpiyskiy National Sports Complex is a multi-use sports and recreation facility in Kiev, Ukraine, on the slopes of Cherepanov Hill in Pechersk Raion.\n- The UEFA Euro 2012 Final took place on 1 July 2012 at the Olympic Stadium in Kiev, Ukraine, to determine the winner of UEFA Euro 2012.\n- Spain defeated Italy 4–0 in the UEFA Euro 2012 Final, a notable match in the Italy–Spain football rivalry.",
